[
	// ============================================================================================================
	// COMPOST FROM BARK (BarkPlan/E06, T06.01). The MAIN sink for surplus ordinary bark: compost demand is
	// effectively unbounded (it feeds soil-compost -> terra preta, consumed by the bucket), so this is where a
	// player sitting on a hundred bark actually burns it off. Modelled on vanilla survival/recipes/barrel/compost.json
	// (rot 64 L -> compost x16, seal 480 h) but deliberately WORSE than rot: rot is pure waste (spoilage that would
	// otherwise vanish) while bark has real alternative uses (tinder, tannin, tar, rope, dye), and bark-mulch
	// composts slowly in reality too, so the higher cost is honest, not a nerf for its own sake.
	//
	// MATCHED BY TAG `bark-compost` (never a code): every kind of bark carries it EXCEPT the two tanning states
	// (bark.json tagsByType), so ordinary, birch, bast, medicinal AND any foreign mod's bark all compost with this one
	// line. Still UNLIKE the pit-kiln sink (T06.02, which matches by code to keep precious birch out of the fire):
	// composting any of these is a fine player choice, exactly the same logic as bark burning as tinder (bark.json)
	// — cooking birch into tar is the smarter use, but wasting it on compost is the player's call, not a trap that
	// eats it by accident.
	//
	// TANNING BARK IS THE ONE EXCLUSION (AuditFixPlan/T08.01, finding F-L7-01). This recipe used to match the umbrella
	// `bark`, so its match set CONTAINED weaktannin-bark.json's and stole from it: 16 tanning bark plus a bucket of
	// water sealed into 2 compost, never tannin. Load order alone does not explain it and renaming this file would not
	// have fixed it. Tannin's bark and water are CO-DRIVERS locked to 1:1 (BarrelRecipe.GetOutputSize demands one
	// identical multiplier from every non-consume ingredient), whereas the consume-water below only asks
	// `waterStack >= consumeLitres * mul` — so this recipe matches bark:water ratios tannin cannot reach and wins
	// outright, before BEBarrel.FindMatchingRecipe's first-match rule is even consulted. Two disjoint tags are the only
	// clean separation. The alternatives on the table (a `quantity` coprime with the tannin working amounts 5 and 7, or
	// making water a co-driver here too) either leave the sets overlapping or force the player to measure water to the
	// litre.
	//
	// ENGINE SHAPE — bark is the QUANTITY driver, water is a consumed liquid. Exact precedent: leather.json
	// (strongtanninportion litres+consumeLitres + hide quantity -> leather stackSize):
	//   * Output game:compost is a NON-LIQUID stack (no waterTightContainerProps), so it lands in the item slot and
	//     the liquid ingredient MUST use consumeLitres — BarrelRecipeIngredient documents consumeLitres as "should
	//     only be used by recipes with a non-liquid output". (Contrast the mod's tannin recipes, whose LIQUID output
	//     forbids consumeLitres; that concern is the mirror image and does not apply here.)
	//   * Bark, a plain item, is measured by `quantity` (ResolveLiquidProperties only converts litres->quantity for
	//     items with liquid props). It is the SOLE co-driver, so output = compost.stackSize * (barkStack /
	//     bark.quantity) (BarrelRecipe.GetOutputSize). Water is not a driver, it only has to satisfy
	//     waterStack >= consumeLitres*ItemsPerLitre * mul; leftover water stays in the liquid slot (TryCraftNow).
	//   * Vanilla codes are game:-qualified because this file lives in the immersivewoodworking domain
	//     (memory vs-mod-asset-path-domain): bare `compost`/`waterportion` would resolve to immersivewoodworking:.
	//
	// NUMBERS are DRAFT (finalised by the T06.04 live check): 8 bark + 2 L water -> 1 compost, seal 480 h. That is
	// ~2x rot's input per unit of compost (rot yields ~1 compost per 4 rot) PLUS a water requirement rot does not
	// have, keeping rot clearly the better composter (DoD "гниль остаётся выгоднее коры"). Seal is kept EQUAL to
	// rot's 480 h so bark is punished on input, not doubly on time. Hardcoded pending the E08 config pass.
	//
	// `code` reuses the vanilla "compost" (a pure grouping string, BarrelRecipe.Code) so the bark route groups under
	// the ONE vanilla compost handbook entry the player cycles through, and the output item is the vanilla compost —
	// indistinguishable from a rot-made one (DoD "неотличим от ванильного").
	// ============================================================================================================
	{
		code: "compost",
		sealHours: 480,
		ingredients: [
			{ type: "item", tags: ["bark-compost"], quantity: 8 },
			{ type: "item", code: "game:waterportion", litres: 2, consumeLitres: 2 }
		],
		output: { type: "item", code: "game:compost", stackSize: 1 }
	}
]
